  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYour income tax return is due today if today is April 15, which is the standard deadline for individual income tax returns in the Philippines.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe NIRC mandates that individual taxpayers must file their income tax returns by April 15, unless this date falls on a weekend or holiday, in which case the deadline may be extended to the next business day. This requirement applies to all individual taxpayers, including those earning compensation income and self-employed individuals.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIf you are an individual taxpayer and today is April 15, you must ensure that your income tax return is filed today to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. If you have not yet filed, consider submitting your return electronically or through an authorized agent bank to meet the deadline.",
